    {
      "source": "RevertIQ",
      "text": "TiFi protocol on BNB Chain was exploited on 10 December 2022 due to spot price manipulation via its use of on-chain AMM reserves for price feeds. The attacker manipulated a liquidity pool’s reserves to inflate the value of collateral and extracted approximately $44,000 in tokens through a sequence of lending and swaps. The TiFi protocol relied on the spot price from a manipulable AMM liquidity pool to determine collateral and loan value. The attacker manipulated BNB-BUSD pool reserves to inflate borrowing capacity and drain protocol tokens."
